# {{PROJECT_NAME}} — Theming

What can be changed without changing code, what cannot, and exactly how much of the appearance a
new theme actually moves.

The claim a theming document exists to make is *"change these values and everything follows"*. That
claim is only worth anything if it is **measured** rather than asserted — see §5. A semantic role
that nothing reads changes nothing when a theme changes it, and a document that lists such roles as
theming surface is making a promise the code does not keep.

Owned by whoever owns the token source. Must change whenever a role is added, removed, or rewired.

